This file is seek.def, from which is created seek.c.  It implements
bbash's "seek" builtin: a clearer-interface wrapper around grep, backed by
POSIX regcomp/regexec (glibc's regex engine) so the matching power is the
same real basic/extended regex support grep itself uses -- the interface
gets simpler, not the matching engine.  This is a brand-new builtin name
that does not exist in stock Bash and touches no existing command.

